

## 🏗️ Technical Architecture (UML Component Diagram)

The system follows a service-oriented architecture where the background service handles critical telemetry while the GUI provides the user interface and AI orchestration.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Industrial Environment"
        MD[Modbus TCP Device / PLC]
    end

    subgraph "Modvera Background Service (logger_service.py)"
        MC[Modbus Client]
        LOG[Logger Loop]
        DB_SQL[(SQLite Database)]
        LIVE_JSON[live_data.json]
        HLT[Health Monitor]
    end

    subgraph "Modvera GUI Dashboard (main.py)"
        UI[UI Thread]
        LVW[Live Viewer]
        RPT[Report Generator]
        AI_P[AI Panel]
    end

    subgraph "Artificial Intelligence (Anthropic)"
        CLAUDE[Claude-3.5 Sonnet API]
    end

    %% Data Flow
    MD <-->|Polling/TCP| MC
    MC --> LOG
    LOG -->|Atomic Write| DB_SQL
    LOG -->|Atomic Update| LIVE_JSON
    HLT -->|Self-Check| LOG

    LIVE_JSON -.->|Read| LVW
    DB_SQL -.->|Query| RPT
    LVW --> UI
    RPT --> UI

    %% AI Flow
    UI --> AI_P
    AI_P -->|Current Readings| CLAUDE
    CLAUDE -->|Situational Analysis| AI_P
    AI_P -->|Turkish Report| UI
```

## 🔄 AI Data Analyst Flow (FBD Style)

This logic diagram shows how data is transformed from raw Modbus registers into actionable AI insights.

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Inputs"
        R1[Register 40001]
        R2[Coil 00001]
        R3[Input 30005]
    end

    subgraph "Processing Logic"
        direction TB
        F1[Normalization]
        F2[Alias Mapping]
        F3[JSON Snapshot]
    end

    subgraph "AI Catalyst"
        PROM["Prompt Builder"]
        ANAL["Claude AI Engine"]
    end

    subgraph "Outputs"
        DISP["GUI Dashboard"]
        REPT["Situation Report"]
        ADVI["Operator Advice"]
    end

    R1 & R2 & R3 --> F1
    F1 --> F2
    F2 --> F3
    F3 --> PROM
    PROM --> ANAL
    ANAL --> REPT
    REPT --> DISP
    REPT --> ADVI
```

